.Dd January 25, 2026
.Dt DEVICE_REGISTER 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm device_register
.Nd register a device with a bus
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/device.h
.In kern/bus.h
.Ft int
.Fn device_register "struct device *dev" "struct bus_type *bus"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn device_register
function registers a device with a specific bus. It adds the device to the bus's list of devices.
.Pp
The function performs the following checks:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Verifies that the device is not already registered with a bus.
.It
Checks for duplicate device pointers in the bus list.
.It
Checks for name collisions with existing devices on the bus.
.El
.Pp
Registration is protected by the bus's spinlock.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn device_register
function returns 0 on success.
.Pp
It returns -1 if:
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Fa dev
or
.Fa bus
is NULL.
.It
The device is already registered.
.It
A duplicate device or name collision is detected.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr device 9 ,
.Xr bus 9 ,
.Xr device_create 9 ,
.Xr device_unregister 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn device_register
kernel interface first appeared in Substrate.
